+# Round B3b — notification templates: the editor page and the grade-detail card
+
+**Status:** PLANNING · Mode: Tier 3, **UI-tester step deferred to the residuals round** (Q91a: the AppHost cannot serve, so a browser hunt would be theatre) · Provider: **pi**
+Orchestrator/plan: `ollama-cloud/glm-5.3-flash` · Plan gate: `ollama/glm-5.3:cloud` · Worker: `ollama-cloud/deepseek-v4.1-flash:1017` · Diff gate: `ollama-cloud/deepseek-v4-pro:0813` · Acceptance: `deepseek-v4-pro:0813` · UI tester: **none this round** — `ollama-cloud/beam` runs in the residuals round over both B2b and B3b
+Branch: `feat/notification-templates-b3b` off `main` (`aacaae60`) · Spec: `documents/specs/assignment-notification-templates.md` §3.10, §3.11, §3.2, §5
+
+Owner rulings folded: **Q79** (B3 before Spec B) · **Q80** (B3 split; this is B3b) · **Q90** (the tag set moves to the shared kernel) · **Q91** (the AppHost diagnosis and the browser pass are residual work; B3b ships on bUnit evidence, recorded as such).
+
+**Plan-review history:** iteration 1 — REWORK (2 P1, 5 P2): the editor was specced as a single-record page although B2c made a slot a **set** (which would have left the constraints editor and conflict warning unreachable), and the §3.11 deep link had a **sending** end but no **receiving** one → folded. Iteration 2 — **ACCEPT** (5 P2, no P1): selection state and the empty/all-constrained slot states pinned, the `?grade=` filter reworded to B3a's `AppliesToGrade` semantics, the constraint `Value` encodings pinned to `AssignmentTemplateContext`, the preview DTO + enum-name travel + sample-fixture/link specified, the preview client's wire-test home named, and the stale `SchoolCollab.Core` mentions corrected to `Core.Abstractions`. **The ≤2 bound is spent**; the round proceeds to the worker on the owner's approval, with no third gate run.
+
+## Substrate inventory (taken before planning)
+
+| Question | Answer found | Consequence |
+|---|---|---|
